            question: "9. What should an air data test set calibration certificate contain?",
            answer: "Instrument identification and serial number; the reference standards used and their own traceability; environmental conditions during calibration; as-found and as-left data at each point on each channel; the stated measurement uncertainty with its coverage factor; the decision rule applied, including any guard banding; the date performed and the next due date; and the authorised signatory. Anything missing is worth querying.",
